# rule.forbid.domain-term-ambiguity

one word, one concept. a term overloaded across two or more senses is forbidden in a contract (dobj/dop name, internal shape, published api/sdk/cli).

test: *does this word name exactly ONE concept, everywhere it appears?* no → one repair is owed:

| the senses differ by… | repair |
|---|---|
| concept (two things) | **split**: keep the word for its primary sense; coin and itemize a term for each other |
| context (one concept, two boundaries) | **qualify** (`rule.require.boundary-qualified-terms`); no coinage |

sort by *"$word, of WHAT?"*: two answers → qualify · one answer, two referents → split.

enumerate the senses of the word you keep BEFORE the inconsistency settles.

blocker: a term overloaded across distinct concepts in a contract · an inconsistency settled with no check that the kept word was also overloaded.
false positive: a boundary-qualified pair (`route.guard.rung` vs `tool.skill.rung`) · generic english · a synonym (that is `rule.forbid.domain-term-synonyms`).
